# One rule, one purpose: the shebang fixture must arrive with CRLF line endings
# on EVERY checkout, on every platform.
#
# An interpreter line that ends `\r\n` is what actually breaks the test runner's
# inline transform (`SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token`, charged to the
# importing test file, which then collects zero tests). The same line ending `\n`
# happens to survive. On Windows, with core.autocrlf=true, every shebanged file in
# the tree already has the breaking shape — so the fixture that proves the cure
# must have it too, deterministically, instead of depending on whose machine
# checked it out.
scripts/sma/__tests__/fixtures/shebang-module.mjs eol=crlf

# The ledger record of a real failure, kept as EVIDENCE — so it must arrive on every
# checkout exactly as it was written, byte for byte. With core.autocrlf=true a checkout
# would hand it back with CRLF and the copy would stop being equal to the original it was
# taken from; the digest that certifies «this is the real record and not a lookalike»
# would then be true on the machine that took it and false everywhere else.
daemon/__tests__/fixtures/ledger-one-attempt-two-outcomes.jsonl eol=lf
